# claude-todo release-signing keys, in git's allowed_signers format (see ssh-keygen(1),
# "ALLOWED SIGNERS"): one `<principal> <key-type> <base64-key>` line per key.
#
# `todo-lock.py update` verifies a release tag against THIS installed copy of the file, never the
# one in the release it is fetching, so a new key is trusted only if a release signed by an old key
# ships it. `release.sh` signs every tag and refuses to release while this file holds no key.
# Rationale: docs/update-trust-decision-2026-09-20.md in the claude-todo repo.
